# Line endings: always LF, on every platform.
#
# core.autocrlf=true is common on Windows and rewrites the working tree to
# CRLF on checkout. That breaks these scripts twice over: "#!/usr/bin/env bash\r"
# is not a valid interpreter path, and the CR survives into the string literals
# patches/apply.py splices into Rust sources.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.jpg binary
*.zip binary
*.keystore binary
